This visualization is based on the provided dinosaur dataset of 292 species across 11 body shapes. Most dinosaurs were medium-sized, about 1 to 9 metres long. Meat-eaters like T. rex grew to around 10 metres. Only the long-necked dinosaurs (sauropods) grew bigger than 12 metres, and the longest, Argentinosaurus and Supersaurus, reached about 28 metre
